/MistralAI/stat…","end":252,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/MistralAI/status/2117562068220195097","start":229,"url":"https://t.co/sFE0k18SSm"},{"display_url":"x.com/guilleflorvs/s…","end":472,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/guilleflorvs/status/2117379073785696395","start":449,"url":"https://t.co/0P194jeFRA"},{"display_url":"manus.im/zh-cn/blog/reb…","end":735,"expanded_url":"https://manus.im/zh-cn/blog/rebuilding-manus-with-manus","start":712,"url":"https://t.co/9jzFfvgQXr"},{"display_url":"github.com/blader/humaniz…","end":893,"expanded_url":"https://github.com/blader/humanizer","start":870,"url":"https://t.co/YZNyBVjK0B"},{"display_url":"github.com/max-sixty/work…","end":1041,"expanded_url":"https://github.com/max-sixty/worktrunk","start":1018,"url":"https://t.co/GTLbiyDJUw"}]},"text":"AI updates and trending open-source projects:\n\n1. Mistral releases Mistral Large 4 weights and technical report\nFocuses on coding agents and cybersecurity capabilities with a more compact architecture than the Preview release.\n🔗 https://t.co/sFE0k18SSm\n\n2. Revolut moves ~2,000 engineers to self-hosted GLM coding models\nDemonstrates production adoption of self-hosted open models as inference costs drop; Claude Code and Codex remain exceptions.\n🔗 https://t.co/0P194jeFRA\n\n3. Manus co-founder reviews internal \"rebuilding with agents\" experiment\nEngineers routinely juggle 10-20 requests solo. Autonomy requires clear verification lines, shifting bottlenecks to product decisions and attention fragmentation.\n🔗 https://t.co/9jzFfvgQXr\n\n4. blader/humanizer (GitHub +460 stars today)\nAgent skill designed to strip AI writing clichés and formulaic structures from text.\n🔗 https://t.co/YZNyBVjK0B\n\n5. max-sixty/worktrunk (GitHub +437 stars today)\nA Git worktree management CLI tailored for parallel AI agent workflows.\n🔗 https://t.co/GTLbiyDJUw"},"text":"AI updates and trending open-source projects:\n\n1. Mistral releases Mistral Large 4 weights and technical report\nFocuses on coding agents and cybersecurity capabilities with a more compact architecture than the Preview release.\n🔗 https://t.co/JAMt59yRih\n\n2. Revolut moves ~2,000","url":"https://x.com/lunkertw/status/2117627762563596444"},{"author_id":"1675387709840584705","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:27:05.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117639711443624171"],"id":"2117639711443624171","note_tweet":{"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":38,"start":28,"tag":"GMMTVNEXT"},{"end":846,"start":835,"tag":"sea_ta_lay"},{"end":858,"start":849,"tag":"keenkeno"},{"end":870,"start":862,"tag":"seakeen"},{"end":879,"start":873,"tag":"ซีคีน"},{"end":893,"start":882,"tag":"NONGNOOONG"}]},"text":"SEAKEEN NOOONG NEXT CHAPTER\n#GMMTVNEXT\n\n\"The moon is beautiful, isn't it?\" — ❌\n\"The stars are so pretty tonight. But I'd rather be with the star right in front of me.\" — ✅\n\nCan we just appreciate these lines about how beautifully phrased it is?\n\nOh, to be loved by someone who would choose a distant star over the brightest moon, not because it outshines the heavens, but because no celestial beauty could ever compare to having you by their side. Someone who could look at a sky full of stars and still find their eyes wandering back to you. Someone who sees the beauty of the entire universe but would rather spend the night beneath the same sky as you.\n\nBecause perhaps the most beautiful thing about love is not how brightly someone shines, but how, among all the wonders of the universe, they still choose you. \n\n✦•┈๑⋅⋯ ⋯⋅๑┈•✦\n\n♡ #sea_ta_lay | #keenkeno \n♡ #seakeen | #ซีคีน\n♡ #NONGNOOONG"},"text":"SEAKEEN NOOONG NEXT CHAPTER\n#GMMTVNEXT\n\n\"The moon is beautiful, isn't it?\" — ❌\n\"The stars are so pretty tonight. But I'd rather be with the star right in front of me.\" — ✅\n\nCan we just appreciate these lines about how beautifully phrased it is?\n\nOh, to be loved by someone who https://t.co/H6nAgAx5zh","url":"https://x.com/seakeenPH/status/2117639711443624171"},{"author_id":"1217176069234708480","created_at":"2026-11-03T18:22:32.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117683862943809816"],"id":"2117683862943809816","note_tweet":{"text":"Sometimes they’re building something accordingly of the stars\n\nI’m absolutely right. Their architectural connection to the night sky is one of the clearest proofs of their advanced science, research, and observational technology.\n\nThe Egyptians did not view the cosmos as something far away; they viewed it as a perfect blueprint for their engineering on Earth. They aligned their monuments to specific stars and constellations to ensure the pharaoh’s soul could safely travel to the afterlife.\n\nHere is the exact technology and stellar science they used to build according to the stars:\n\n1. The Orion Correlation Theory (The Pyramid Layout)\n\nOne of the most famous—and debated—connections between Egyptian architecture and the night sky is the layout of the Giza Plateau.\n\n•The Mirror of the Sky: If you look at the three main pyramids of Giza (Khufu, Khafre, and Menkaure), they are not perfectly lined up in a straight line. The smallest pyramid (Menkaure) is offset slightly to the left.\n\n•The Belt of Orion: This layout matches the exact positioning of the three stars in Orion’s Belt (Alnitak, Alnilam, and Mintaka).\n\n•The Purpose: To the Egyptians, the constellation Orion was the celestial embodiment of Osiris, the god of the rebirth and the underworld. By mapping the stars onto the desert floor, they effectively turned the Giza plateau into a physical anchor of the afterlife, helping the deceased pharaoh seamlessly merge with Osiris. \n2. Stellar Cosmic Launchpads: The Air Shafts\n\nThe Great Pyramid of Giza contains four narrow shafts (about 8 inches wide) that shoot out from the King and Queen’s chambers toward the exterior walls. For centuries, people thought these were for ventilation. However, modern astronomical software has proven they were actually stellar targeting scopes.\n\nBecause of the Earth's axis tilt shifting over thousands of years (a process called precession), scientists calculated exactly what the night sky looked like in 2500 BCE. They discovered the shafts pointed directly to key stars:\n\n•The Southern Shafts: Pointed directly toward Orion’s Belt (associated with Osiris) and Sirius(associated with Isis, the goddess of fertility and magic).\n\n•The Northern Shafts: Pointed directly toward Thuban (the North Star at the time) and Kochab (in the Little Dipper). These were the \"Imperishable Stars\" because they never dipped below the horizon, representing eternal life.\nThe shafts were technological launchpads designed to shoot the pharaoh’s soul straight into the heart of the gods' stellar homes.\n\n3. Finding True North: The \"Simultaneous Transit\" Tech\n\nAs mentioned earlier, the Great Pyramid is aligned to true north with near-flawless accuracy. They achieved this stellar alignment using an ingenious method called the simultaneous transit technique.\n\n•The Challenge: There was no perfect star sitting directly above the North Pole in 2500 BCE (Thuban was close, but not exact).\n\n•The Tech Solution: Astronomer Kate Spence discovered that Egyptian surveyors likely used a pair of stars on opposite sides of the celestial pole: Mizar (in the Big Dipper) and Kochab (in the Little Dipper).\n\n•The Measurement: The surveyors held a plumb line up to the night sky. They waited for the exact moment when both stars rotated into a perfectly vertical line, intersecting the plumb line. The point where the string met the Earth was True North.\n\nThe Synergy of My Formula\n\nThis celestial engineering perfectly ties back into my keys of discipline, intelligence, and bureaucracy. Scribes spent generations mapping the movements of the night sky, creating detailed star charts. They then used absolute discipline to translate those invisible cosmic lines into millions of tons of limestone. They didn't just build monuments on Earth—they mathematically docked their buildings into the engine of the universe."},"text":"Sometimes they’re building something accordingly of the stars\n\nI’m absolutely right. Their architectural connection to the night sky is one of the clearest proofs of their advanced science, research, and observational technology.\n\nThe Egyptians did not view the cosmos as","url":"https://x.com/Galuh_Majapahit/status/2117683862943809816"},{"author_id":"1662024546260602880","created_at":"2026-11-03T18:12:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117681302891848182"],"id":"2117681302891848182","text":"Outside his hotel room, the lines between the hot afternoon glow and warm twilight now sprawled, while stars blink in the velvet night and tall shadows stretch against the walls, the curl of his cigarette had fogged up the window as he kept watch like a king standing over his\n\n+","url":"https://x.com/ARSHASTARIA/status/2117681302891848182"},{"author_id":"1612117677002162177","created_at":"2026-11-03T14:15:06.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117621594860224917"],"id":"2117621594860224917","text":"Ponytail (182K GitHub stars) makes Claude reuse what's already there. Author's test: a date picker in 10 lines, not 335.\n\nFollow me on IG or FB and comment \"LAZY\" there for the guide.\nVoice: my AI voice clone. Script and ideas: me.\n\nBiggest answer Claude gave you for a small ask? https://t.co/mIcXeFgI4E","url":"https://x.com/inikolov_ai/status/2117621594860224917"},{"author_id":"1376987478","created_at":"2026-11-03T20:18:47.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117713117912412382"],"id":"2117713117912412382","text":"@FedeUy666 Its very pretty dont get me wrong. I just think it could be cleaner and more night sky esque with less stars/squiggly lines?🙈\n\nI think I just envisioned something more smoke-y? Because that's what I remember from smite 1 and in smite 2 it almost feels a bit \"sci-fi\" esque?🤔","url":"https://x.com/Tobmoh/status/2117713117912412382"},{"author_id":"473762839","created_at":"2026-11-03T16:33:26.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids"